            <ArticleTitle>Successful Treatment of Human Plague with Oral Ciprofloxacin.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3201/eid2303.161212</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The US Food and Drug Administration recently approved ciprofloxacin for treatment of plague (Yersina pestis infection) based on animal studies. Published evidence of efficacy in humans is sparse. We report 5 cases of culture-confirmed human plague treated successfully with oral ciprofloxacin, including 1 case of pneumonic plague.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
